{"ui_id":"u_000002_01","response_id":"r_000002_01","query_id":"q_000002","intent":"Information Retrieval","tags":["travel","itinerary-planning","europe"],"intent_bucket":"information_retrieval","genui_json":[{"version":"v0.9","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"surface_q_000002","catalogId":"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json"}},{"version":"v0.9","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"surface_q_000002","components":[{"id":"root","component":"Column","children":["text_1"]},{"id":"text_1","component":"Text","text":"TITLE: Rome 2-Day Walking Itinerary: Pantheon Base\n\nAssumptions:\n- You have a moderate fitness level and are comfortable with significant walking (15,000-25,000 steps per day).\n- All major attraction tickets will be pre-booked online to guarantee entry and skip long ticket lines. This is essential.\n- The budget of 100 Euros per person per day is for food and scheduled entry fees only, not including souvenirs, extra transport, or shopping.\n- Prices for tickets and food are estimates for 2024 and should be verified.\n\n---\nSECTION: PRE-TRIP CHECKLIST\n\n- Book Colosseum & Roman Forum ticket online for Day 1 (9:00 AM slot).\n- Book Vatican Museums & Sistine Chapel ticket online for Day 2 (8:30 AM slot).\n- Purchase the new Pantheon entry ticket online or plan to queue.\n- Download an offline map of Rome (e.g., Google Maps offline feature).\n- Pack comfortable walking shoes. This is the most important item.\n\n---\nSECTION: BUDGET & TICKET FRAMEWORK\n\nThis is an example breakdown of your daily 100 Euro budget.\n\nTABLE: DAILY BUDGET ESTIMATE\nCategory | Estimated Cost | Notes\n--- | --- | ---\nEntry Fees (Avg.) | €25 | Colosseum (~€20), Vatican (~€25), Pantheon (€5). Averaged over 2 days.\nBreakfast | €5 | Cappuccino and a cornetto at a local bar (standing at the counter is cheaper).\nLunch | €15 | Pizza al taglio (by the slice) or a fresh panino.\nDinner | €40 | A sit-down meal at a trattoria (pasta/pizza, glass of house wine, water).\nSnacks/Gelato | €15 | Includes water, coffee breaks, and essential daily gelato.\n**Total** | **€100** |\n\nHOW TO VERIFY TICKET PRICES & BOOK:\n1. Visit the official websites provided in the 'Sources' section below.\n2. Select your desired date (2024-09-15 for Colosseum, 2024-09-16 for Vatican).\n3. Choose your time slot. Morning slots are highly recommended.\n4. Complete the purchase and save the digital ticket to your phone.\n\n---\nICONS:\n- SIGHTSEEING: https://icon.url/sightseeing\n- FOOD: https://icon.url/food\n- WALKING: https://icon.url/walking\n- TIP: https://icon.url/tip\n\nIMAGES:\n- The Colosseum: https://example.image.url/colosseum\n- St. Peter's Basilica: https://example.image.url/stpeters\n- The Trevi Fountain: https://example.image.url/trevi\n- The Pantheon: https://example.image.url/pantheon\n\nQUICK ACTIONS:\n[Button: Book Colosseum Tickets] coopculture.it\n[Button: Book Vatican Museums Tickets] museivaticani.va\n\n---\nSECTION: ITINERARY DAY 1 (2024-09-15): ANCIENT ROME\n\nFocus: Immerse yourself in the heart of the Roman Empire.\n\nMORNING (8:00 AM - 1:00 PM)\n\n- (SIGHTSEEING) 8:00 AM: Start from your lodging near the Pantheon. Walk towards Piazza Venezia to see the Altare della Patria (Vittoriano). You can view it from the outside to save time and money.\n  - (WALKING) Pantheon to Piazza Venezia: Approx. 10 minutes.\n- (SIGHTSEEING) 8:30 AM: Walk along Via dei Fori Imperiali towards the Colosseum. This road is flanked by the ruins of ancient forums.\n- (SIGHTSEEING) 9:00 AM - 12:00 PM: **Colosseum, Roman Forum & Palatine Hill**.\n  - (TIP) Use your pre-booked 9:00 AM ticket for the Colosseum. The visit takes about 1.5 hours.\n  - After the Colosseum, your ticket gives you access to the adjacent Roman Forum and Palatine Hill. Allow at least 1.5 hours to explore these vast ruins. Start with Palatine Hill for great views over the Forum.\n  - (WALKING) Piazza Venezia to Colosseum: Approx. 15 minutes.\n\nLUNCH (1:00 PM - 2:00 PM)\n\n- (FOOD) Avoid the restaurants directly facing the Colosseum. Walk a few blocks away towards the Monti or Celio neighborhoods for better value and quality.\n\nEXAMPLE LUNCH OPTIONS (CARDS):\nOption 1: Pizza al Taglio | Forno da Milvio | Grab delicious, affordable pizza by the slice. | €10-€15\nOption 2: Quick Panini | La Prezzemolina | Fresh, made-to-order sandwiches perfect for a fast and tasty lunch. | €8-€12\nOption 3: Local Trattoria | Hostaria I Clementini | A short walk away for authentic Roman pasta if you want a sit-down meal. | €20-€25\n\nAFTERNOON (2:00 PM - 6:00 PM)\n\n- (WALKING) 2:00 PM: A gentle stroll past historical sites.\n  - Walk past the Circus Maximus, the ancient chariot racing stadium.\n  - Optional: See the Mouth of Truth (Bocca della Verità) at the nearby church. Expect a queue for photos.\n- (SIGHTSEEING) 4:00 PM: Climb Capitoline Hill.\n  - (TIP) Don't miss the free, spectacular panoramic view over the Roman Forum from the back of the main square (Piazza del Campidoglio), designed by Michelangelo. It's especially beautiful in the late afternoon light.\n  - (WALKING) Colosseum area to Capitoline Hill: Approx. 20 minutes.\n\nEVENING (6:00 PM onwards)\n\n- (FOOD) 7:30 PM: Dinner in the Jewish Ghetto or near Campo de' Fiori, both known for fantastic Roman cuisine.\n- (SIGHTSEEING) 9:30 PM: **Trevi Fountain**.\n  - Walk from your dinner spot to the Trevi Fountain. It is famously crowded but magical when illuminated at night. Toss a coin to ensure your return to Rome.\n  - (WALKING) Capitoline Hill to Trevi Fountain: Approx. 15 minutes.\n\nEXAMPLE DINNER OPTIONS (CARDS):\nOption 1: Roman-Jewish | Nonna Betta | Famous for artichokes \"alla giudia\" in the heart of the Jewish Ghetto. | €35-€45\nOption 2: Classic Pasta | Osteria da Fortunata | Near Campo de' Fiori, watch pasta being handmade in the window. | €30-€40\nOption 3: Budget Pizza | Emma Pizzeria | Excellent thin-crust Roman pizza in a stylish setting. | €25-€35\n\n---\nSECTION: ITINERARY DAY 2 (2024-09-16): VATICAN & RENAISSANCE WONDERS\n\nFocus: Art, architecture, and the splendor of Vatican City and Rome's famous piazzas.\n\nMORNING (8:00 AM - 1:00 PM)\n\n- (WALKING) 8:00 AM: Walk from the Pantheon area across the Tiber River towards Vatican City.\n  - (WALKING) Pantheon to St. Peter's Square: Approx. 25-30 minutes.\n- (SIGHTSEEING) 8:30 AM - 12:30 PM: **Vatican Museums & Sistine Chapel**.\n  - Use your pre-booked 8:30 AM ticket to enter the museums.\n  - Follow the signs on the one-way route. Highlights include the Raphael Rooms, the Gallery of Maps, and the tour's finale, the Sistine Chapel.\n  - (TIP) The visit takes a minimum of 3-4 hours. Do not rush. Photography is forbidden inside the Sistine Chapel.\n- (SIGHTSEEING) 12:30 PM: **St. Peter's Basilica**.\n  - There is a special passage that sometimes connects the Sistine Chapel directly to St. Peter's Basilica, allowing you to bypass the main security line outside. Look for it. If it's closed, you'll have to exit the museums and queue for the Basilica (entry is free, but the security line can be long).\n  - (TIP) Dress code is strictly enforced: knees and shoulders must be covered for both men and women.\n\nLUNCH (1:30 PM - 2:30 PM)\n\n- (FOOD) The area around the Vatican (Prati) has many great, non-touristy food options if you walk 5-10 minutes away from St. Peter's Square.\n\nEXAMPLE LUNCH OPTIONS (CARDS):\nOption 1: Gourmet Street Food | Trapizzino | A unique pizza-pocket filled with classic Roman stews. | €10-€15\nOption 2: Roman Deli | Panificio Bonci | Legendary bakery offering incredible pizza by the slice and baked goods. | €15-€20\nOption 3: Local Favorite | Hostaria Dino e Toni | A no-frills, authentic Roman trattoria loved by locals. | €20-€25\n\nAFTERNOON (2:30 PM - 6:00 PM)\n\n- (WALKING) 2:30 PM: Walk from the Vatican back towards the city center via Ponte Sant'Angelo, the beautiful bridge lined with angel statues, with Castel Sant'Angelo guarding the entrance.\n- (SIGHTSEEING) 3:30 PM: **Piazza Navona**.\n  - Admire Bernini's Fountain of the Four Rivers in this stunning baroque square.\n- (SIGHTSEEING) 4:30 PM: **Pantheon**.\n  - Head to your \"home base.\" Now is the time to go inside. The visit itself is quick (20-30 minutes) but awe-inspiring. Remember the ~€5 entry fee.\n- (SIGHTSEEING) 5:30 PM: **Spanish Steps**.\n  - A short walk from the Pantheon. Climb the steps for a nice view and enjoy the bustling atmosphere of the luxury shopping streets below.\n  - (WALKING) Piazza Navona -> Pantheon -> Spanish Steps is a 15-20 minute walk in total.\n\nEVENING (6:00 PM onwards)\n\n- (FOOD) 7:30 PM: For your final dinner, find a cozy spot near the Spanish Steps or head to the Trastevere neighborhood (a 25-min walk or short bus ride) for a charming, lively atmosphere.\n- (TIP) Enjoy a final evening passeggiata (stroll) through the illuminated streets before concluding your trip.\n\nEXAMPLE DINNER OPTIONS (CARDS):\nOption 1: Trastevere Classic | Tonnarello | Extremely popular spot in Trastevere known for huge portions of classic pasta. | €30-€40\nOption 2: Near Spanish Steps | Ginger. Sapori e Salute | A healthier, modern option with fresh juices, salads, and gourmet dishes. | €40-€50\nOption 3: Hidden Gem | Armando al Pantheon | (Book far in advance) A Roman institution right by the Pantheon for an unforgettable final meal. | €50-€60\n\n---\nSOURCES:\n- Official Colosseum Ticket Vendor: https://www.coopculture.it/en/products/ticket-colosseum-roman-forum-palatine_24h/\n- Official Vatican Museums Tickets: https://tickets.museivaticani.va/home\n- Official Pantheon Information: https://www.pantheonroma.com/home/","variant":"body"}]}}],"assets":[],"toon":"[2]:\n  - version: v0.9\n    createSurface:\n      catalogId: \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\"\n      surfaceId: surface_q_000002\n  - version: v0.9\n    updateComponents:\n      surfaceId: surface_q_000002\n      components[2]:\n        - component: Column\n          id: root\n     