r 13.6-inch Liquid Retina display that is brighter (500 nits vs. 400 nits) and supports 1 billion colors. This display includes a notch for the camera. The M1 Air retains the classic tapered wedge design with a 13.3-inch Retina display.\n*   **Charging and Ports**: The M2 Air brings back the dedicated MagSafe 3 charging port, which frees up its two Thunderbolt / USB 4 ports for accessories even while charging. The M1 Air charges via one of its two Thunderbolt / USB 4 ports.\n*   **Camera and Audio**: The M2 model features an upgraded 1080p FaceTime HD camera, providing a much clearer image than the 720p camera on the M1 model. It also has an improved four-speaker sound system.\n\nImages:\n-   2020 MacBook Air (M1) Design: https://store.storeimages.cdn-apple.com/4982/as-images.apple.com/is/macbook-air-gold-select-201810?wid=904&hei=840&fmt=jpeg&qlt=90&.v=1664472289059\n-   2022 MacBook Air (M2) Design: https://store.storeimages.cdn-apple.com/4982/as-images.apple.com/is/macbook-air-midnight-select-20220606?wid=904&hei=840&fmt=jpeg&qlt=90&.v=1653084303665\n\nQuick Actions:\n[Button: Compare Mac Models on Apple.com] https://www.apple.com/mac/compare/\n[Button: View M2 MacBook Air Tech Specs] https://www.apple.com/macbook-air-13-and-15-m2/specs/\n[Button: View M1 MacBook Air Tech Specs] https://support.apple.com/kb/SP825\n\nSources:\n- https://www.apple.com/newsroom/2022/06/apple-unveils-all-new-macbook-air-supercharged-by-the-new-m2-chip/\n- https://support.apple.com/kb/SP869","variant":"body"}]}}],"assets":[],"toon":"[2]:\n  - version: v0.9\n    createSurface:\n      catalogId: \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\"\n      surfaceId: surface_q_000031\n  - version: v0.9\n    updateComponents:\n      surfaceId: surface_q_000031\n      components[2]:\n        - component: Column\n          id: root\n          children[1]: text_1\n        - component: Text\n          id: text_1\n          text: \"Assumptions:\\nThis comparison is based on the offi