{"ui_id":"u_000051_01","response_id":"r_000051_01","query_id":"q_000051","intent":"weather","tags":["packing-list","forecast-analysis","london"],"intent_bucket":"weather","genui_json":[{"version":"v0.9","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"surface_q_000051","catalogId":"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json"}},{"version":"v0.9","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"surface_q_000051","components":[{"id":"root","component":"Column","children":["text_1"]},{"id":"text_1","component":"Text","text":"Assumptions:\nThis packing list assumes a standard business casual to business formal dress code. It is optimized for a carry-on suitcase and provides gender-neutral suggestions where possible, with specific options noted. The focus is on layering to adapt to the variable weather conditions.\n\nTrip & Weather Overview:\n- Destination: London, UK\n- Dates: 2024-10-15 to 2024-10-17\n- Forecast: Cool, wet, and windy. Temperatures range from 10°C to 14°C with heavy rain and strong winds on the first two days.\n\nIcons:\n- Outerwear: https://icon.url/trench-coat\n- Business Attire: https://icon.url/briefcase\n- Footwear: https://icon.url/boots\n- Essentials: https://icon.url/passport\n- Toiletries: https://icon.url/toothbrush\n\nPacking Checklist\n\n(Outerwear)\nA versatile, weather-resistant outer layer is critical for this trip.\n- [ ] Waterproof Trench Coat or Smart Rain Jacket (x1): Choose a neutral color like black, navy, or beige that works with business attire.\n- [ ] Compact Travel Umbrella (x1): Essential for the heavy rain forecasted.\n- [ ] Wool Scarf (x1): Provides warmth against the wind and adds a professional touch.\n\n(Footwear)\nComfort and water resistance are key. You will likely be walking between transport and meetings.\n- [ ] Waterproof Leather Shoes or Boots (x1 pair): Such as leather Chelsea boots, brogues, or loafers treated with a waterproofing spray. Avoid suede.\n- [ ] Smart Dress Shoes (x1 pair): A second, comfortable pair for indoor meetings or dinners.\n\n(Business Attire)\nFocus on layering and fabrics like merino wool, cashmere, and cotton blends that provide warmth without bulk.\n- [ ] Suit or Blazer/Trousers/Skirt Combo (x2): Choose versatile pieces in navy, grey, or black that can be mixed and matched.\n- [ ] Dress Shirts or Blouses (x3): One for each day.\n- [ ] Fine-Knit Sweater or Cardigan (x2): For layering under a blazer on colder days (Oct 15/16). Merino wool is an excellent choice.\n- [ ] Business-appropriate Trousers or Skirt (x1, extra): A separate item to mix with blazers.\n- [ ] Belt (x1)\n\n(Casual & Basics)\nFor travel, evenings, or any downtime.\n- [ ] Dark Jeans or Chinos (x1 pair)\n- [ ] Casual Shirt or Sweater (x1)\n- [ ] Underwear & Socks (x3 pairs): Consider one pair of wool socks for the coldest day.\n- [ ] Sleepwear (x1 set)\n\n(Essentials)\n- [ ] Passport & Travel Documents\n- [ ] Wallet (with GBP/contactless cards)\n- [ ] Phone & Charger\n- [ ] Laptop/Tablet & Charger\n- [ ] UK Power Adapter (Type G)\n- [ ] Portable Power Bank\n- [ ] Business Cards\n- [ ] Notebook & Pen\n\n(Toiletries)\n- [ ] Toiletry Bag with travel-sized essentials (toothbrush, toothpaste, deodorant, etc.)\n- [ ] Skincare/Moisturizer (wind can be drying)\n- [ ] Any personal medications\n\nPacking Tip\nLay out all your items before packing to ensure they coordinate. Roll clothing items to save space and prevent wrinkles in your carry-on. Keep your umbrella and rain jacket easily accessible for your arrival on a rainy day.\n\nImages:\n- Key Outerwear: A classic waterproof trench coat is ideal for London's business scene and weather. https://image.url/london-trench-coat\n- Appropriate Footwear: Waterproof leather Chelsea boots are stylish, comfortable, and practical. https://image.url/chelsea-boots\n- Essential Tech: A UK Type G power adapter is non-negotiable for your electronics. https://image.url/uk-adapter\n\nQuick Actions:\n[Button: Shop UK Travel Adapters] https://www.example.com/electronics/travel-ada