{"ui_id":"u_000721_01","response_id":"r_000721_01","query_id":"q_000721","intent":"Education","tags":["study-plan","test-prep","mathematics"],"intent_bucket":"education","genui_json":[{"version":"v0.9","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"surface_q_000721","catalogId":"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json"}},{"version":"v0.9","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"surface_q_000721","components":[{"id":"root","component":"Column","children":["text_1"]},{"id":"text_1","component":"Text","text":"Assumptions:\n- You have access to SAT Math study materials (textbooks, practice tests, online resources).\n- \"Problem Solving\" will be integrated throughout the schedule, as it's a skill applied to all content areas.\n- The 1 hour on weekdays is for focused learning and practice, and the 3 hours on Saturdays are for review, practice tests, and deeper dives.\n\nSAT Math 4-Week Study Schedule\n\nThis schedule is designed to cover the core SAT Math topics with a focus on Algebra, Problem Solving, Data Analysis, and Passport to Advanced Math. Each weekday session is approximately 1 hour, and Saturday sessions are 3 hours.\n\nWeek 1: Heart of Algebra & Problem Solving\n\nDay | Focus Area | Specific Topics\n----|------------|----------------\nMonday | Linear Equations | Solving linear equations (one variable), word problems involving linear equations.\nTuesday | Systems of Equations | Solving systems of linear equations (substitution, elimination, graphing), word problems.\nWednesday| Linear Inequalities | Solving linear inequalities, graphing on a number line, systems of linear inequalities.\nThursday | Interpreting Linear Functions | Understanding slope, intercepts, rate of change, and interpreting linear functions in context.\nFriday | Functions Basics | Function notation, evaluating functions, domain and range, basic linear function graphs.\nSaturday | Week 1 Review & Practice | Comprehensive review of Week 1 topics. Timed practice set on Algebra, analyze errors.\n\nWeek 2: Problem Solving and Data Analysis\n\nDay | Focus Area | Specific Topics\n----|------------|----------------\nMonday | Ratios, Proportions, Percentages | Setting up and solving ratio, proportion, and percentage problems, including word problems.\nTuesday | Rates & Unit Conversions | Solving problems involving rates, unit conversions, and proportional relationships (direct/inverse variation).\nWednesday| Data Interpretation | Reading and interpreting data from tables, charts, and graphs; calculating basic statistics.\nThursday | Statistics Concepts | Mean, median, mode, range, and conceptual understanding of standard deviation.\nFriday | Probability | Basic probability concepts, simple and compound events, conditional probability.\nSaturday | Week 2 Review & Practice | Comprehensive review of Week 2 topics. Timed practice set on Data Analysis, analyze errors.\n\nWeek 3: Passport to Advanced Math\n\nDay | Focus Area | Specific Topics\n----|------------|----------------\nMonday | Polynomials | Operations with polynomials (addition, subtraction, multiplication), factoring simple quadratics.\nTuesday | Quadratic Equations | Solving quadratic equations (factoring, quadratic formula, completing the square).\nWednesday| Functions & Graphs | Graphing parabolas, identifying roots/vertex, understanding function transformations.\nThursday | Exponential Functions & Radicals | Exponential growth/decay, properties of exponents, simplifying and operating with radicals.\nFriday | Rational Expressions & Equations | Simplifying rational expressions, solving basic rational equations.\nSaturday | Week 3 Review & Practice | Comprehensive review of Week 3 topics. Timed practice set on Advanced Math, analyze errors.\n\nWeek 4: Comprehensive Review & Full Practice Tests\n\nDay | Focus Area | Specific Topics\n----|------------|----------------\nMonday | Targeted Practice: Algebra | Focused practice on identified weak areas from Week 1 & 2 Algebra topics.\nTuesday | Targeted Practice: Data Analysis | Focused practice on identified weak areas from Week 2 Data Analysis topics.\nWednesday| Targeted Practice: Advanced Math | Focused practice on identified weak areas from Week 3 Advanced Math topics.\nThursday | Full SAT Math Practice Test | Take a full, timed SAT Math section practice test (70 minutes).\nFriday | Practice Test Review | Thoroughly review Thursday's practice test. Understand every incorrect answer, revisit relevant topics.\nSaturday | Second Full SAT Math Practice Test | Take another full, timed SAT Math section practice test. Final review of common mistakes and strategies.\n\nGeneral Tips:\n- Use official College Board SAT practice tests for the most accurate preparation.\n- Keep an error log: For every question you get wrong, write down the topic, why you got it wrong, and the correct approach.\n- Don't just practice; understand. Focus on the underlying concepts, not just memorizing formulas.\n- Simulate test conditions during practice tests (timed, no distractions).\n- Review formulas and common mathematical properties regularly.\n\nQuick Actions:\n[Button: Find Official SAT Practice Tests] https://satsuite.collegeboard.org/sat/practice-preparation/free-sat-practice-tests\n[Button: Explore Khan Academy SAT Prep] https://www.khanacademy.org/sat","variant":"body"}]}}],"assets":[],"toon":"[2]:\n  - version: v0.9\n    createSurface:\n      catalogId: \"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json\"\n      surfaceId: surface_q_000721\n  - version: v0.9\n    updateComponents:\n      surfaceId: surface_q_000721\n      components[2]:\n        - component: Column\n          id: root\n          children[1]: text_1\n        - component: Text\n          id: text_1\n          text: \"Assumptions:\\n- You have access to SAT Math study materials (textbooks, practice tests, online resources).\\n- \\\"Problem Solving\\\" will be integrated throughout the schedule, as it's a skill applied to all content areas.\\n- The 1 hour on weekd