{"ui_id":"u_000362_01","response_id":"r_000362_01","query_id":"q_000362","intent":"Localization","tags":["travel","itinerary","dining"],"intent_bucket":"localization","genui_json":[{"version":"v0.9","createSurface":{"surfaceId":"surface_q_000362","catalogId":"https://genui.local/specification/v0_9/standard_catalog.json"}},{"version":"v0.9","updateComponents":{"surfaceId":"surface_q_000362","components":[{"id":"root","component":"Column","children":["text_1"]},{"id":"text_1","component":"Text","text":"Assumptions:\n  - The trip dates 2025-05-15 to 2025-05-20 imply 5 full days of activities (May 15th, 16th, 17th, 18th, 19th), with May 20th being a departure day. The itinerary covers these 5 activity days.\n  - The budget of $50 per person per meal is for a main course and perhaps a drink/side, not including very expensive extras or alcohol.\n  - Travel within Tokyo will primarily be via its efficient public transport system (trains/subways).\n\nYour 5-day Tokyo itinerary focusing on Shinjuku and Shibuya is outlined below, along with restaurant recommendations.\n\nTokyo 5-Day Itinerary: Shinjuku & Shibuya Focus\n\nDay-by-Day Plan:\nDay 1: Thursday, May 15, 2025 - Shinjuku Arrival & Gardens\n  Morning: Arrive in Tokyo, check into your accommodation in Shinjuku or Shibuya.\n  Afternoon: Shinjuku Gyoen National Garden - Enjoy a peaceful stroll through this beautiful imperial garden.\n  Late Afternoon: Tokyo Metropolitan Government Building - Head to the free observation decks for panoramic views of Tokyo.\n  Evening: Dinner in Shinjuku. Explore Shinjuku Golden Gai or Omoide Yokocho (Piss Alley) for a glimpse into traditional Tokyo nightlife and small eateries (for atmosphere, not necessarily dinner).\n\nDay 2: Friday, May 16, 2025 - Shibuya Icons & Views\n  Morning: Shibuya Crossing & Hachiko Statue - Experience the iconic scramble crossing and meet the famous loyal dog statue.\n  Afternoon: Shibuya Sky - Ascend to the rooftop observation deck for breathtaking 360-degree views of the city. Explore Shibuya Center Gai for trendy shops.\n  Evening: Dinner in Shibuya. Enjoy shopping around Shibuya 109 and other department stores.\n\nDay 3: Saturday, May 17, 2025 - Shinjuku Shopping & Culture\n  Morning: Shinjuku Shopping Spree - Explore major department stores like Isetan, Takashimaya Times Square, and Lumine EST for a mix of high-end and trendy Japanese fashion.\n  Afternoon: Samurai Museum (optional) - Immerse yourself in the history of the samurai. Alternatively, explore the quieter side streets of Shinjuku.\n  Evening: Dinner in Shinjuku. Discover the vibrant atmosphere of Kabukicho (Shinjuku's entertainment district) without necessarily engaging in its nightlife.\n\nDay 4: Sunday, May 18, 2025 - Harajuku Fashion & Meiji Jingu\n  Morning: Meiji Jingu Shrine - Visit this serene Shinto shrine dedicated to Emperor Meiji and Empress Shoken, located in a large forested area.\n  Afternoon: Harajuku Exploration - Dive into Takeshita Street for quirky fashion and sweets, then stroll Omotesando for upscale boutiques and cafes. Wander down Cat Street for unique finds.\n  Evening: Dinner in Harajuku or return to Shibuya/Shinjuku. Consider a themed cafe experience if interested.\n\nDay 5: Monday, May 19, 2025 - Modern Art & Departure Prep\n  Morning: TeamLab Planets TOKYO (Toyosu) - Experience an immersive digital art museum. (Note: This requires a short train ride from Shinjuku/Shibuya to Toyosu. Book tickets in advance.)\n  Afternoon: Last-minute Souvenir Shopping & Packing - Grab any final gifts or items you might have missed in Shinjuku or Shibuya.\n  Evening: Farewell Dinner - Enjoy a final memorable meal in one of your favorite districts.\n\nRestaurant Recommendations (Budget: ~$50 per person per meal)\n\nThese are EXAMPLE recommendations. Prices and availability can vary.\nTo verify live info: Check restaurant websites or use booking platforms like TableCheck, Hot Pepper Gourmet, or OpenTable for current menus, prices, and reservations.\